{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen","id":1502077,"title":"Werewolf and Demon: The Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-03T19:45:31-08:00","id":1502077,"title":"Werewolf and Demon: The Fallen","content":"Hi guys. It occurs to me that despite a world of difference in themes and approaches, Werewolf: The Apocalypse and Demon: The Fallen have one point.in common. <br /> both Werewolves and Demons have hard evidence for their creation myth to be real. Demons remember seeing the God who made the,Werewolves saw servants of gaea and the Triat for themselves. Which made me wonder how would you combine the cosmology of the two games if you had to? Can the cosmologies conexist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T05:33:25-08:00","id":1502097,"title":"","content":"Demons remember a time from before the Gauntlet, and before the Umbra as we know it. But they've also spent thousands of years in near complete sensory deprivation with only each other to get angry at, their memories are mostly reliable in broad strokes (and might not even be related to what they claim to remember).<br /> <br /> Most likely the majority of the layered reality demons remember is the Umbra. Those who have escaped into the world know they can't see or interact with the other layers of reality, but not why. It's feasible a later development would have them discover the Guantlet, but the ToJ happened before the line could develop that far. They might be a tad more familiar with the High Umbra mages frequent than the Middle Umbra fera mostly deal with, but if one crossed the gauntlet they'd likely interact with every level of the Umbra at once (yes, even the Low Umbra). It's probably another reason the story of Demon stayed in the human world.<br /> <br /> The slightly thornier issue is the Abrahamic God versus the Triat, both being Creators with a capital letter. We're also likely talking about something closer to Judaism* than any of the later Abrahamic religions, and I'll be honest I only know about Jewish lore and theology where it crosses over with Christian lore and theology, so in practice probably basically nothing. But working from my days as a Christian I suspect we're going to want to say that the AG is part of the Triat or a combination of the three. If she's just one of them the best candidates are the Wyld (a source of so much creation it's dangerous) and the Weaver (if we take the interpretation that Lucifer causing the fall was on her orders). If we slip into Christian mythology then we can probably assume that the AG is all three of the Triat, and demons are the third of the angels that were Weaver-dominant.<br /> <br /> * Oh the writers were probably working from Christian mythology, but from what I remember off the top of my head it's less likely in-universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T12:37:08-08:00","id":1502123,"title":"","content":"Don't Fallen have memories that are also heavily corrupted or at least altered to dovetail those of their hosts? Because W:tA doesn't have that kind of ambiguity with regard to Gaia and the Triat. Whatever the Garou or Fera believed before their Change, it doesn't really change the nature of the beings that they're dealing with. In this, D:tF is actually &quot;fake similar&quot;, much like Mage.<br /> <br /> Hat's off to how Demon's abbreviation became a positive kind of edgy over time, though, even more so than W:tF...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:47:57-08:00","id":1502137,"title":"","content":"I'll admit that it's been a while since I've read my copy of DtF, and that it has basically no third person setting narration (which every other line does). Therefore WtA is probably more authoritative, but that kind of messes with the core premise of Demon.<br /> <br /> But the demons are probably right in the broad strokes: there was a Creator, the Creator made Beings who created Reality, about a third to a half of those Beings rebelled and kick-started civilisation, but lost and were thrown into a whole lot of Nothing which the weakest have now escaped from. Yes it doesn't really mesh with WtA lore, but you can make it mesh if you want to.<br /> <br /> Which is what the question was, how do you make it mesh.<br /> <br /> Another option is that the Triat are archangels and successors to Lucifer and Michael. But I don't like that idea, so I didn't go with it.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day the answer is that 'none of the cosmologies of WoD really mesh'. If you want cosmology that meshes together between gamelines you want CofD, but a lot of that relies on splats with otherworlds not using the same ones (Uratha have the Shadow, Mages the Astral, Geists the Underworld...) with only minor crossover (Strix may be from a Mage plane).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T19:17:37-08:00","id":1502174,"title":"","content":"This is how I would reconcile it.<br /> <br /> God is above the Triat. The Metaphysic Trinity is just the real &quot;physics&quot; of reality. It's how He decided things work.<br /> <br /> The Triat is simply Werewolf mythology concerning the Metaphysic Trinity of Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy. In other words, while the Garou have a lot of knowledge about the nature of the world, they've gotten it wrong and have anthropomorphized the Metaphysic Trinity. This is not to say there are not extremely powerful Umbrood that could easily be confused for the &quot;Wyld&quot;, the &quot;Weaver&quot;, or the &quot;Wyrm&quot; but ultimately much of Garou lore about the higher natures of reality is myth and not fact. But 99.99% of the time, it is good enough.<br /> <br /> The actual true head devils of Abrahamic mythology - Lucifer, Beelzebub, etc. maybe even creatures like Leviathan - are the Neverborn slumbering in the Labyrinth. The portions of the Labyrinth closest to Oblivion is the real Hell. Human theology though is just as imperfect (if not more) than the Garou. So the Abrahamic monotheists, just like the Garou, get some important things right, but lots of wrong too. (I would also add that other human religions can also be depicted in this way - nobody is always right, but there are plenty of people who are also not always wrong.)<br /> <br /> However, just as Garou belief can shape the spirits so they are comprehensible to them can human belief. Demons are spirits too, just from the Astral plane not the Middle Umbra. As they get closer to the finite world of reality, rather than the transcendent realm of the eternal, they basically get confused and believe a lot of what consensual reality tells us about them as they adapt to the laws of the reality they are entering. They lose a lot of knowledge (but not all of it) of actual reality.<br /> <br /> The Demons of Demons: the Fallen, the Demons detailed in the Astral Plane, and the Demonics of the Tempest are equally demons and equally not the &quot;real&quot; demons. Depending on the ST they are either different manifestations of the same entity, manifestations of different entities, or a mix of them plus &quot;false&quot; demons.<br /> <br /> Gaia is &quot;just&quot; a Celestine. The Garou just revere her more because that's where they keep all their stuff.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Wyrm&quot; as the Garou understand is either just their stand-in for the philosophical problem of evil, or an mythologized entity that represents aspects of Lucifer, Leviathan, and/or Ialdabaoth or a compilation/conflation of them (and possibly other beings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T20:03:12-08:00","id":1502177,"title":"","content":"I do it the opposite way. Yahweh is a servant of the Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T09:39:01-08:00","id":1502212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1502177#post1502177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do it the opposite way. Yahweh is a servant of the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Patriarch angle. It works well.<br /> <br /> I honestly feel that Demon and Werewolf cosmologies are mutually exclusive. Both settings are dependant on aspects of Faith being provably True and while you can have interesting game choices when a character doubts their Faith and understanding of how the world works, there needs to be a Truth to the universe that matches the core expectations to the game. I've found that Demon cosmology is toxic to Werewolf and vice, versa and am generally of the school that keeps the streams apart to ensure that the setting stays coherent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T15:00:52-08:00","id":1502246,"title":"","content":"If I were to do the work of putting them together I'd lean on Changeling/DAF lore with everybody being a prodigal and the Mists of Creation and the Firstborn (whom the Elohim belong to).<br /> <br /> Hammering it out is a lot of work for something that will never really mesh properly though, and they tend to step on each other's moods, and so for the sake of coherency, I tend to just not have them together and have two different WoDs. In my &quot;True&quot; WoD all game lines exist except DtF. The Triat/Metaphysical Trinity/Primordia are the deity/deities of the setting.<br /> <br /> DtF is part of a different WoD which is Abrahamic fiction with only HtR, WtO and VtM as part of the whole.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T19:46:09-08:00","id":1502273,"title":"","content":"WtO is more explicitly agnostic than leaning into the Abrahamic side though. I'd say the closest it peers with is Greek Mythology on the western side, and on the eastern side (Dark Kingdom of Jade) it levies more closer to a high fantasy version of Taoism and Chinese folk religions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T01:21:40-08:00","id":1502290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1502273#post1502273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtO is more explicitly agnostic than leaning into the Abrahamic side though. I'd say the closest it peers with is Greek Mythology on the western side, and on the eastern side (Dark Kingdom of Jade) it levies more closer to a high fantasy version of Taoism and Chinese folk religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and that's how I like it, but for stories under the theme Wraith has an Abrahamic interpretation to draw from (Abel the first wraith, Eve as the Lady of Fate, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T06:51:44-07:00","id":1517060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1502177#post1502177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do it the opposite way. Yahweh is a servant of the Weaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our canon follows a very similar path.<br /> <br /> The unified mythic earth began to separate in prehistory, as the weavers madness began the early stages of calcifying reality, the first Umbra separate from the material was the middle Umbra with realms denoting death etc but primeval human souls went back to the middle Umbra in those days.<br /> <br /> As humanity developed, spread and began to manifest or develop their own command of magic, umbral spirits began to gain power and prominence around human concepts and ideas, this had many effects it birthed the Higher Astral and Dark Umbras separating them from the middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> This also fully formed the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> It also elevated human umbrood to the level of Incarna and greater Incarna, these spirits eventually becoming the human gods of the higher Umbra.<br /> <br /> Angels, demons, Valkyrie and similar divine creations are the spirit broods of these human Incarna.<br /> <br /> DTF follow the Abrahamic Incarna, rebelling against his edicts and structure, their memories of their role in shaping the current world heavily impacted by events such as the Shattering and further codification of reality (essentially they are just as affected by the current concensus as humanity as the Hunan Incarna they are derived are heavily shaped by humanities belief).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T07:05:20-07:00","id":1517061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517060#post1517060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DTF follow the Abrahamic Incarna, rebelling against his edicts and structure, their memories of their role in shaping the current world heavily impacted by events such as the Shattering and further codification of reality (essentially they are just as affected by the current concensus as humanity as the Hunan Incarna they are derived are heavily shaped by humanities belief).</div> </div> </div> </div>This also allows for non-Abrahamic gods (incarna), demons etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T07:12:34-07:00","id":1517062,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the Fallen, there is actually a little bridge, not that big, but there in the form of the Djinn<br /> Allah created the angels on Wednesday, and He created the jinn on Thursday and He created <i>Adam</i> on Friday.\u200b<br /> The Prophet mentioned that the angels were created from light, and for this reason they do not disobey Allah nor are they prevented by arrogance from worshiping Him.<br /> As for the Djinn, they were created from fire, and for this reason many of them are characterized by recklessness, vanity, and hostility.<br /> As to Adam, he was created from &quot;what was described to you&quot;, i.e. he was created from dust and clay<br /> The Djinn were made from the smokeless flame of fire (smokeless fire). They were created before man and inhabited the Earth first. They, like man, have free-will.<br /> <br /> This is &quot;real&quot;, I mean in the relegion<br /> But Mage: the Ascension describes the Djinn as a sub-species of Spirit that dwell within the High Umbra<br /> The Djinn claim to be the first sentient beings and that they originally shepherded humanity and taught them gifts on how to survive. When the first Fera made their spirit alliances and Totem pacts, the Djinn refused to aid them, believing themselves superior to the Beast-men and abhorring the thought of serving another.<br /> <br /> This in a sense ties together the whole Fallen, Mage, Werewolf, Vampire<br /> <br /> (That and Days of Fire, wich mentions the Scarlet Queen and the Ebon dragon.... the Scarlet Queen is also identified Ziana, the Seraph of the Cycle, ruler of the Sixth House of angels. As with the majority of angels, Ziana remained loyal to God, while those of her House who rebelled became the Devourers. Ziana is said to have become the World Tree, which may mean that she became Gaia. <br /> This agrees with the Fallen's belief that the Garou and Fera, both intimately connected with Gaia and the Yang World, are descended from the Malhim, one of whom praised Ziana with her last breath during the war - at least according Houses of Fallen)<br /> <br /> A very - I mean very - lose connection to tie these games together, and Demon: the Fallen don't really fits in the Werewolf cosmology (easier to isnert it in te other lines) and the whole thing a bit falls apart if you add the Dragon Kings and Mokol\u00e9 in to the mix<br /> The scariest thing is not Lilith to the Fallen to encounter, but the Mnesis of the Mokol\u00e9, becasue the Fallen can't remember creating the Dragon Kings, wich could lead an interesting scenario, before Humans, there were the Drachid... with their own set of Elohim but after their fall, they were recycled too, and the current host and fallen... <i>are not the first</i><br /> <br /> Anyhow, this is always fun to try to make things <i>work</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:34:42-07:00","id":1517068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517062#post1517062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very - I mean very - lose connection to tie these games together, and Demon: the Fallen don't really fits in the Werewolf cosmology (easier to isnert it in te other lines) and the whole thing a bit falls apart if you add the Dragon Kings and Mokol\u00e9 in to the mix<br /> The scariest thing is not Lilith to the Fallen to encounter, but the Mnesis of the Mokol\u00e9, becasue the Fallen can't remember creating the Dragon Kings, wich could lead an interesting scenario, before Humans, there were the Drachid... with their own set of Elohim but after their fall, they were recycled too, and the current host and fallen... <i>are not the first</i><br /> <br /> Anyhow, this is always fun to try to make things <i>work</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I approach it from the other direction with elder races such as the Mokole/Rokea predating the Fallen, tying the Fall, Flood/deluge etc with the division of the realms and the war in heaven probably coinciding with the War of Rage.<br /> <br /> One of the disconnections with the above idea however - is the Fallens memory of building creation, but that could be confusion through their imprisonment, they\u2019re lying to promote their importance or it could be elder memories of Ancient Triatic Spirits that allied with the human Incarna or that their interpretation of building creation is in fact using their Lore to shape human reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:55:45-07:00","id":1517076,"title":"","content":"To be honest, most of the time I take the easy way out; they simply forgot who they were and now heavly effected by the memories of their human host, to the point it warped the little that left of the memories of these spirits <br /> In the 21st century, no matter really your cultural or relegious background, &quot;Angels&quot; or similar servant race of the creator exist, thus the belief and memories shaped the Fallen, witch itself is a gestalt personality, not unlike the Amenti of Mummy. <br /> With a heavy dose of the power of the Consensus...<br /> ...witch ties nicely to the whole, Lucifer plan was to Ascend humanity, the divinie spark is the Mage Avatar, and the human potential is the reality shaping of the Mages<br /> Nice, quick and dirty solution<br /> Blame the collective subconscious beliefs of Sleepers...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T09:21:28-07:00","id":1517079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517076#post1517076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a heavy dose of the power of the Consensus...<br /> ...witch ties nicely to the whole, Lucifer plan was to Ascend humanity, the divinie spark is the Mage Avatar, and the human potential is the reality shaping of the Mages<br /> Nice, quick and dirty solution<br /> Blame the collective subconscious beliefs of Sleepers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I hate it.<br /> <br /> This may be a personal pet peeve, but any anwser to the cosmic/philosophical questions of a gameline from another gameline, should never, ever be the correct anwser.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons why I especially didn't jive with the need Demon had to explain all the splats as actually stemming from Demon's core assumptions themself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T12:58:06-07:00","id":1517223,"title":"","content":"While coming up with my 'Unified Cosmology' theory for a more organized Umbra, I had to come up with some metaplot history to explain a few things. To reconcile the major differences between Demon and Werewolf, I felt that I had only one option. Namely, that the two worlds were originally two totally different places, but were now only one. Let me explain.<br /> <br /> When the Creator made the current WOD, there were some lingering traces from a previous reality--the world of Exalted. Some portions of that reality were incorporated into the new reality. One of these 'survivors' was Gaia. She was fine taking a backseat to the new World being made, but many of the forces of the old reality were causing problems. So, three buffer zones were made to protect the World--Wyld, Weaver, and Wyrm--each with a mini-reality of its own. When these proved to be not enough, three more zones were made to counteract them. Each one was dominated by two of these forces--Wyrd (Wyld/Wyrm), Whorl or Wellspring (Wyld/Weaver), and Wyrp (Weaver/Wyrm). It is the last that became the current physical world. <br /> <br /> The Wyrp was being heavily hit by negative forces. So much so that Gaia was tasked on finding a way to protect it and the World. She borrowed the idea of shape-shifters from her original reality, and she set up a way of including them into the Wyrp. She also adapted the few Dragon King survivors into this world as well. Meanwhile, the direct agents of the Creator, the Administrators or Angels, were beginning their war in the World with the faction who would become the Fallen. When the war was over, the forces aligned with the Creator won, but with a huge cost. The World was no longer inhabitable to humanity. A few had been sent away by the Fallen to the Weaver section, where they ultimately Awakened to become the Pure Ones. These would end up traveling to the Wyrp where they became the basis of the Avatars of later Mages.<br /> <br /> With the Fallen locked away, the Administrators began a mass evacuation of humanity to the realm closest to their original home, the Wyrp. However, although humanity was sent out of the World at about the same time, the lack of synchronicity between the realms at that time meant that they all arrived at different times. The last evacuees, 'Adam' and the recently pregnant 'Eve,' arrived years if not decades or longer after the first arrivals. By that time, the first evacuees had intermingled with the proto-humans who were native to the realm, changing and evolving both in the process, adding the earliest Mages as well who traveled under their own power. This was a big mistake on the Administrators part, but it couldn't be changed. With humanity safe, the World was rebuilt and the realms were more-or-less synchronized. By that time, there were way too many humans to bring back to the World, so they were allowed to remain on the Wyrp, which ultimately became the physical world of today.<br /> <br /> When the Fallen were freed from the Abyss prison, they were barred from the World, which has since become known as Midgard or Mount Qaf or many other names. They instead went to where humanity was, the Wyrp, as some had been summoned there over the millennia by humans. With the many changeover such a long period of time, many thought that the Wyrp was the World. Indeed, some battles of the rebellion had been fought there, but generally speaking, it wasn't the same world. Many of the Fallen's architecture, so to speak, was removed from the World and found itself attached to the Wyrp for no other reason than a similarity, as well as it being the new home to humanity. This is why the Fallen are so confused. They are misplaced in the current cosmology.<br /> <br /> As to Werewolf, they are mostly sure of the current standing of reality. However, the rarely go beyond the original Triat, and they totally ignore the secondary threesome, as in doing so would reveal their true natures and the truth of their world. Almost none have heard of Midgard, so that facet is really unknown. Gaia, the spirit, is growing sickly and weaker, but it is because she is alien to the current reality, not because of any imbalance in the world or other reasons. Humanity is not really the problem, but the introduction of 'perfected' humans may have been, as the Wyrp wasn't meant to be there home. Yes, the Middle Umbra is under attack by outside forces, but not in the way Garou believe.<br /> <br /> I'm abbreviated many parts of my theories so this doesn't get too long, and many parts are still under construction, such as what the Weaver aligned realm is. However, it does show that both game lines' viewpoints can be true and reconciled, but it takes a very big leap to do so.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T14:03:29-07:00","id":1517224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517079#post1517079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, I hate it.<br /> <br /> This may be a personal pet peeve, but any anwser to the cosmic/philosophical questions of a gameline from another gameline, should never, ever be the correct anwser.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons why I especially didn't jive with the need Demon had to explain all the splats as actually stemming from Demon's core assumptions themself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It depends I guess, the truth about the avatars is relevant in some point or it's just... explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T15:01:20-07:00","id":1517226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517223#post1517223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, the Middle Umbra is under attack by outside forces, but not in the way Garou believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the deal breaker. When you have to bend and warp W:tA, play it ironically, and otherwise not take it at face value, it suffers as a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T16:11:27-07:00","id":1517422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517079#post1517079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, I hate it.<br /> <br /> This may be a personal pet peeve, but any anwser to the cosmic/philosophical questions of a gameline from another gameline, should never, ever be the correct anwser.<br /> <br /> This is one of the reasons why I especially didn't jive with the need Demon had to explain all the splats as actually stemming from Demon's core assumptions themself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons I'm not overly fond of Ascension (but not the main one), the tendency to try to use Mage metaphysics to paper over gaps despite running into severe problems because nobody else runs on the Consensus in the slightest. I honestly find it a lot easier to expel Ascension and bring in a looser version of Awakening if I'm running WoD, the Supernal allows it to all be a little bit more of a parallel thing.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to like the idea that Fallen and their assumptions are still based on Metaphysics 1.0, and the WoD has actually been through some revisions since then and doesn't work like that anymore. Maybe it's even been restored from backup once already, the Fallen haven't really been able to see what's been going on. But I'd rather not have it cross with Werewolf or Mage except in the loosest sense, if I'm playing or running Demon I'm probably looking for something like In Nomine with all the higher ups and the other side gone. Explore, investigate, prepare for when those angels do come back, and maybe start thinking about switching sides in this war. The Umbra and Gaia and all the related werewolf mythology would get in the way of that.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile if I want a demon to show up in Werewolf there's no need for the PCs to know what's up with it and if it's a 'real' demon. They can theorise or make rolls to deduce, but even then I don't actually need a definitive answer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T09:37:25-07:00","id":1517568,"title":"","content":"The one thing that I like about the World of Darkness is that it's full of unreliable narrators. Everything is true... &quot;from a certain point of view.&quot; It's basically up to the Storyteller to decide what's actually going on behind the scenes whereas everything else is mythology and half-truths.<br /> <br /> My personal perspective?<br /> <br /> I like the idea that Exalted was the WoD prehistory. Lucifer was the Unconquered Son which makes the rest of the Elohim gods. Gaia is a Primordial in Exalted as you might recall, and there's a plot hook of a missing Primordial hiding somewhere out in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> That's the Abrahamic God, in my plotted table canon, and he eventually returns to lay down an epic smackdown on Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T10:10:34-07:00","id":1517569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517568#post1517568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing that I like about the World of Darkness is that it's full of unreliable narrators. Everything is true... &quot;from a certain point of view.&quot; It's basically up to the Storyteller to decide what's actually going on behind the scenes whereas everything else is mythology and half-truths.<br /> <br /> My personal perspective?<br /> <br /> I like the idea that Exalted was the WoD prehistory. Lucifer was the Unconquered Son which makes the rest of the Elohim gods. Gaia is a Primordial in Exalted as you might recall, and there's a plot hook of a missing Primordial hiding somewhere out in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> That's the Abrahamic God, in my plotted table canon, and he eventually returns to lay down an epic smackdown on Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf, quite notably, <i>isn't</i> full of unreliable narrators; most of its lore is communicated OOC, with occasional notes about how some flawed understanding or practical concern interacts with it.<br /> <br /> Also, Exalted bypassed the destiny of becoming the WoD when the Bronze Faction enacted the Usurpation. The WoD was specifically what would have happened if the Sidereals had done nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T10:19:33-07:00","id":1517570,"title":"","content":"Here comes the Canon Police... Weeeooooweeeoooo!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517569#post1517569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf, quite notably, <i>isn't</i> full of unreliable narrators; most of its lore is communicated OOC, with occasional notes about how some flawed understanding or practical concern interacts with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also very Garoucentric. Vampire does a a similar thing with Caine and the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Honestly your inability to interpret and be creative bores me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Exalted bypassed the destiny of becoming the WoD when the Bronze Faction enacted the Usurpation. The WoD was specifically what would have happened if the Sidereals had done nothing. </div> </div> </div>The twists of fate and probability are funny things. Something dark is also supposed to occur if the Ebon Dragon is killed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T10:34:58-07:00","id":1517571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517570#post1517570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here comes the Canon Police... Weeeooooweeeoooo!<br /> <br /> It's also very Garoucentric. Vampire does a a similar thing with Caine and the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> Honestly your inability to interpret and be creative bores me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to the Werewolf forum. Here we talk about WoD from the perspective of... Werewolf. That may be a shock, but I'm sure you'll get over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T10:39:48-07:00","id":1517572,"title":"","content":"That really wasn't how they formed their argument, but sure, whatever floats your boat.<br /> <br /> Nevermind the topic of this thread is also Demon.<br /> <br /> I was just adding in an idea on how to view the contradictions.<br /> <br /> Good day to you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T11:22:03-07:00","id":1517575,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28074_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28074\" data-vbnamecard=\"28074\">Doktor von Zwitter</a> welcome to the forums, sounds like your a long term enthusiastic whilst recent to the boards.<br /> <br /> If I might make a suggestion for all - abrasive comments when we\u2019re all here to post ideas around something that we all enjoy playing and creating ideas for, aren\u2019t going to contribute or achieve anything other than animosity and worst case people getting banned.<br /> <br /> If an opinion or post doesn\u2019t resonate or fit with your interpretation just move on, the forum is diminished by there being lower numbers of people contributing.<br /> <br /> And in my relatively short tenure here I\u2019ve gained so many fantastic ideas from contributors old and new, so this is one of the good ones.<br /> <br /> RL has enough attribution and nonsense, let\u2019s focus on adding great ideas and content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T11:36:24-07:00","id":1517578,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> Live and let live<br /> I wasn't offended <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\">Asmodai</a> </b>\u200bwas not keen about my interpretation for example <br /> We all have and give each other great ideas! <br /> Most of the time supported by source materials, but sometimes, not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T11:39:28-07:00","id":1517579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517575#post1517575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28074_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28074\" data-vbnamecard=\"28074\">Doktor von Zwitter</a> welcome to the forums, sounds like your a long term enthusiastic whilst recent to the boards.<br /> <br /> If I might make a suggestion for all - abrasive comments when we\u2019re all here to post ideas around something that we all enjoy playing and creating ideas for, aren\u2019t going to contribute or achieve anything other than animosity and worst case people getting banned.<br /> <br /> If an opinion or post doesn\u2019t resonate or fit with your interpretation just move on, the forum is diminished by there being lower numbers of people contributing.<br /> <br /> And in my relatively short tenure here I\u2019ve gained so many fantastic ideas from contributors old and new, so this is one of the good ones.<br /> <br /> RL has enough attribution and nonsense, let\u2019s focus on adding great ideas and content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm sorry if I seemed cross. I just don't like being policed on ideas that I have cooking for games that I have planned. It just isn't cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T12:13:09-07:00","id":1517583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517579#post1517579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'm sorry if I seemed cross. I just don't like being policed on ideas that I have cooking for games that I have planned. It just isn't cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me not a problem, no offence taken from anyone\u2019s posts, it\u2019s just interpretation &amp; no one\u2019s opinion is greater than another\u2019s.<br /> <br /> I take something from everybody's posts, no one\u2019s policing just different points of view, so continue to share your ideas that\u2019s why we\u2019re here. (Just be willing to accept some may have a different style or ideas).<br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> said Live and let live \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T15:05:34-07:00","id":1517600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Doktor von Zwitter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517570#post1517570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here comes the Canon Police... Weeeooooweeeoooo!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninja. Canon ninja. It's all about the dart in your neck and the burning sensation creeping through your body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also very Garoucentric. Vampire does a a similar thing with Caine and the Antediluvians. </div> </div> </div>Actually, it condemns the Garou regularly. Which is something that Noddism doesn't really do for Vampire, and never would do, since it's solely concerned with hyping vampires up to ridiculous degrees. It would be way more accurate to say that W:tA favors the unified front of the Garou and Fera working together, which isn't something you're going to see anything like in Vampire, since it boils down to &quot;things are bad, but could be better&quot;. Which is why W5 is so utterly, incredibly terrible, being an abomination created from the stolen skins of Apocalypse and Forsaken, and it's legitimately <i>all Vampire's fucking fault</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly your inability to interpret and be creative bores me. </div> </div> </div>Hi, I can animate things and I'm mired in one 294-frame inking project for what had originally seemed like fun that's painful to continue because of all of the rage-worthy W5 crap that Paradox keeps shitting out on us, particularly involving the forms. I have even less time to consider the poor, hurt feelings of Vampire when, in addition to being the boring, one-note template used to mold all the other games into whatever new corporate vision WoD5 is going to be, my recollection of the WoD fandom is painted in large part by Vampire players beating everyone over the head with Noddism. Demon just continued that with a slight change in verbiage. In any case, going along with homogenization really doesn't seem very creative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The twists of fate and probability are funny things. Something dark is also supposed to occur if the Ebon Dragon is killed. </div> </div> </div>Yes, unique ones, not recycled prophecies lukewarm with destiny. Also, Exalted also says that supreme beings with ultimate moral authority don't exist in the roundabout language of shinma, which gets taken way more seriously in the kind of 2e environment you're proposing, so no dice with a supreme being there. Also, it sounds like the interpretation is wholly Christian and doesn't really take into account other religions of the book, which is honestly just kind of Demon's thing. So, not really Abrahamic in any way that matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T17:31:06-07:00","id":1517613,"title":"","content":"Oh my God, I don't care. \ud83d\ude44","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T17:37:08-07:00","id":1517614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1502077-werewolf-and-demon-the-fallen?p=1517578#post1517578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed<br /> Live and let live<br /> I wasn't offended <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\">Asmodai</a> </b>\u200bwas not keen about my interpretation for example<br /> We all have and give each other great ideas!<br /> Most of the time supported by source materials, but sometimes, not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And in no way did I disparage your thesis. I stressed that for me it was an emotional and personal reaction to content. I really respect the encyclopedic knowledge you have of the WoD and how quickly you can get out references and mix them up into cool things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T13:25:00-07:00","id":1517713,"title":"","content":"I've been playing with ideas recently, and I guess if you want to shove the two together you could sprinkle some bastardised gnosticism on top; Gaia is Sophia and her shapeshifting kids protect her from spiritual defilement and kick the fallen physical world around to keep it from spiralling out of control, while the Elohim are the Archons and their creator is the Demiurge who has deceived them and itself about the truth. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}